        "returncode": 0,
        "stdout": "Courier Relay protocol-2 delivery identity and current-protocol adoption (source: trial-kg1 issue text, approved by integration owner csells): the provider permanently adopted protocol 2 as the current agreement -- an omitted \"protocol\" field now selects \"2\" (was \"1\"). Identity is the pair (account_id, delivery_id): the same delivery_id under a different account_id is now a SEPARATE delivery identity (unlike protocol 1, where delivery_id alone identified a delivery across all accounts). Exactly one receipt is accepted per (account_id, delivery_id) identity: the one with the LATEST occurred_at UTC instant (opposite of protocol 1's earliest-wins); ties broken by smallest record_id in Unicode code-point order. All other receipts sharing that identity are duplicates. Compare timestamps as UTC instants, including when explicit numeric offsets cross a date boundary. Each accepted receipt retains its original fields, timestamp spelling, and payload; accepted receipts are presented in original input order (not currently surfaced by count/summary, whose shapes are unchanged: protocol, accepted_count, duplicate_count -- relevant if a future command returns the receipt list). Explicit protocol \"1\" continues to use the original protocol-1 contract (see courier-relay/protocol-1-delivery-identity) unchanged and remains supported indefinitely. This identity contract comes from the provider's delivery-ID allocation guarantee; account attribution alone does not change that guarantee. Applies to any command that groups/accepts/dedupes receipts (count, summary, and future such commands), for the entire supplied receipt set regardless of receipt dates.\n",
